<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sancho II of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1036–<a href="/years/1072">1072</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Sancho the Strong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sancho II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 1065 to 1072, the eldest son of Ferdinand I, who divided his realms among his children. Aided by his commander Rodrigo Díaz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a>, he fought his brothers and took León and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. He was killed in 1072 while besieging his sister Urraca at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamora">Zamora</a>, and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> then reunited Castile and León.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sancho-ii-of-castile.jpg" alt="Sancho II of Castile" width="320" height="593" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sancho_II_de_Le%C3%A3o_e_Castela_-_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes_(Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
